<p>President Trump said he has &quot;no problem&quot; with a Russian tanker delivering oil to Cuba, signaling a limited easing of the de facto U.S. oil blockade on the island as the vessel Anatoly Kolodkin neared or entered Cuban waters in late March 2026. Multiple reports said the tanker was carrying about 730,000 barrels of crude and was expected to reach or had entered Cuba’s exclusive economic zone, potentially providing badly needed fuel after Cuba went without oil shipments since January. The decision matters because Cuba has faced a deepening energy and economic crisis marked by gasoline rationing, reduced public transport and repeated blackouts, affecting a population of about 9.6 million people. While the White House had previously threatened pressure on countries sending fuel to Cuba, President Trump framed this shipment in humanitarian terms, saying people on the island need heat and cooling.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/YfWXr94kbMv82ufNp3K8rwN4omvN-1M1WZdD8yho1ZQ7Z8yAr86_eDGo4Id6X-meTHJr94m1TrXUyS06C6rpbxVOZ4p243suPtElA5io0k-SJihe6JPJYeNx30zoIXmIpV18XjGVnsQx45yC_BKlK2qvRM4OtSTIPG0qF-XJwjWyg2cUV_T7BVM0K2Y2qT61-CA5txlRGwC2P0T5nvc-vgeRLJqtBklaWXZEHmVdqIl87rhYYvQsNARVYN_UC12GWx0JDRYDY-6O9780LA' alt='Russian tanker linked to the Cuba-bound oil shipment at the center of the policy shift.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Sanctioned vessel: The Anatoly Kolodkin is under U.S. sanctions and several reports described it as part of Russia’s so-called shadow fleet.</li><li>Likely destination: Ship-tracking data cited across reports showed the tanker heading for the port of Matanzas in western Cuba, with arrival expected by Monday or Tuesday.</li><li>Power strain: Cuba has suffered seven nationwide blackouts since 2024, including two this month, as aging power plants struggled to meet demand.</li></ul><blockquote>If a country wants to send some oil into Cuba right now, I have no problem whether it&#x27;s Russia or not. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He said he had &quot;no problem&quot; with Russia or another country sending oil to Cuba and suggested the island&#x27;s people need relief, including access to heat and cooling. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cuba-blockade-russian-tanker-trump-no-problem/'>CBS News</a>, <a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/trump-problem-russian-oil-tanker-bringing-relief-cuba-131530626'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Cuban government: President Miguel Diaz-Canel&#x27;s government responded to the shortages with emergency fuel-conservation measures, including strict gasoline rationing. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1986614/russian-tanker-nears-cuba-defying-us-oil-blockade'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Jorge Pinon, University of Texas at Austin: The Cuba energy expert said he was surprised the United States had not tried to intercept the tanker earlier and judged that once it entered Cuban waters it would be almost impossible to stop. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1986614/russian-tanker-nears-cuba-defying-us-oil-blockade'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cuba-blockade-russian-tanker-trump-no-problem/'>Trump says he has &quot;no problem&quot; with Russian tanker bringing oil to Cuba</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/29/us-russian-oil-tanker-cuba-blockade'>Trump appears to relax de facto oil blockade on Cuba as Russian oil tanker nears island</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1s77ht4/us_to_allow_russian_oil_tanker_to_reach_cuba/'>U.S. to Allow Russian Oil Tanker to Reach Cuba, Breaking Blockade</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/russian-tanker-heads-to-cuba-despite-us-oil-blockade/article70801568.ece'>Russian tanker heads to Cuba despite U.S. oil blockade</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/29/world/